#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Without it, `clang-tidy <file>` runs whatever checks the
# invoker typed, so two people auditing the same file reach different lists and
# neither is the project's. The list below is the project's.
#
# THE CHECKS THAT ARE OFF ARE THE POINT. Each one is off for a reason recorded
# here, because a check disabled without a reason gets re-enabled by the next
# person who runs `-checks=modernize-*` and wonders why the tree disagrees.
#
# modernize-use-trailing-return-type
#   WebKit's rule is "only use the arrow for function return types if it allows
#   you to omit redundant information". This check applies the arrow
#   unconditionally, to every declaration in the tree. Selective is the rule; a
#   blanket rewrite is not a stricter version of it, it is a different rule.
#
# modernize-return-braced-init-list
#   It rewrites `return std::string(1, c);` to `return {1, c};`, which is not the
#   same expression: braces prefer the initializer_list<char> constructor, so the
#   result is the two characters 0x01 and c. Applied to keyTokenForCodePoint,
#   it formats every letter key with a 0x01 in front of it. Nothing failed to compile and the printf output looked
#   correct, because the stray byte is invisible until you print the length.
#   The check cannot see which constructor the braces will select, so its fixit
#   is a guess wherever a type has a list constructor.
#
# modernize-use-designated-initializers
#   Measured 2026-07-30: 84,842 sites, of which 82,579 are in four generated
#   .tables.inc files that a generator rewrites wholesale. Fixing generated
#   output is churn the next generator run deletes.
#
# modernize-use-auto
#   `auto` where the type is not spelled on the right-hand side hides it from
#   the reader, and this check does not distinguish the two cases.
#
# modernize-loop-convert
#   Its fixit needs manual repair on every run, measured across three: it names
#   the element after the INDEX it replaced, so a loop over `bool[]` becomes
#   `for (bool& i :` and `i` survives into a body that indexes nothing — 21 sites
#   in one run, 4 in another, 3 in a third. It also leaves the `sizeof` count
#   constant behind, unused under -Werror, four times. Neither is visible to the
#   check, and a range-for is worth having only where a person picked the name.
#
# modernize-avoid-c-arrays
#   WANTED, and not enabled yet. The check ships NO fixits (measured: 3
#   diagnostics, 0 replacements), so every conversion is hand work, and ~320
#   sites remain. Enabling it now would mean a config the tree does not satisfy.
#   Three groups are not conversions to std::array at all and are excluded when
#   it is turned on: a `static constexpr char x[] = "literal"` wants
#   std::string_view, the generated tables are rewritten by their generator, and
#   `const char* const argv[]` is execv's ABI.

Checks: >
  -*,
  clang-diagnostic-ignored-attributes,
  modernize-concat-nested-namespaces,
  modernize-macro-to-enum,
  modernize-min-max-use-initializer-list,
  modernize-raw-string-literal,
  modernize-redundant-void-arg,
  modernize-use-bool-literals,
  modernize-use-emplace,
  modernize-use-equals-delete,
  modernize-use-nodiscard,
  modernize-use-nullptr,
  modernize-use-override,
  modernize-use-ranges,
  modernize-use-scoped-lock,
  modernize-use-starts-ends-with,
  modernize-use-std-numbers,
  modernize-use-std-print,
  modernize-use-using

# A diagnostic in a header is reported once per translation unit that includes
# it, so a Core header reached by 200 TUs reports 200 times. Deduplication is
# the reader's problem either way; what this controls is which headers are ours.
#
# POSIX ERE, which has no lookahead. llvm::Regex accepts `(?!…)` without a word
# of complaint and then matches nothing, so a filter written in PCRE suppresses
# every header diagnostic and the run reports a header-heavy tree clean. The
# exclusion below is what keeps ThirdParty out, and it is a separate option
# precisely because this one cannot express it.
HeaderFilterRegex: '(Source|Tests)/.*\.h$'

# ThirdParty is vendored, and a fix applied there is reverted by the next
# vendor update. Generated tables are rewritten by their generator.
ExcludeHeaderFilterRegex: '(ThirdParty|\.tables\.inc)'

FormatStyle: file
